reply.body:
Yep, what @bpintea said that was my thinking as well. Date math is a bit special as we never want to create blocks of an other type than `DATETIME`. So, the only time when we want to have arithmetics between date periods or time durations is when folding constants.

@costin, I can probably extract this into block friendly code, but I think that will create additional complexity that might not be warranted. Currently, the evaluators for date math are based on the fact that a date time block will be added to a constant value (see[ evaluator definition here](https://github.com/elastic/elasticsearch/blob/aff49dc69a489a40f2aa4a2ae8c31b3c4825b2a8/x-pack/plugin/esql/src/main/java/org/elasticsearch/xpack/esql/expression/predicate/operator/arithmetic/Add.java#L87-L89)); so, making the date math logic block based will likely require bigger changes.

If that's okay with you, @costin , I'd prefer not to block-ify the duration/period arithmetics. I think I can put the code for the actual arithmetics into the corresponding operator class, though (`Add.java` and `Sub.java`), then at least all processing code is nicely in one place, even if the code for processing periods/durations does not generate an evaluator.

